An individual user can create a variable called TZ, but for system wide
use cd as root to /etc/zoneinfo, which has a data file for most time
zones. There create a symbolic link called localtime to the data file
of your choice. 

I.e., ln -s /etc/zoneinfo/localtime -> /etc/zoneinfo/GB-Eire

A user's TZ variable will override the localtime link.
-- 

                             Jeff Wilson

