chrisho@hotmail.com wrote in message <3907da66.18156800@news.starhub.net.sg>...
>Hi all,
>
>I have a Digital Unix 4.0D server.
>We use a mirror script to replicate files from this server to another
>one.
>
>Every so often, the mirror would fail because the password for the
>account would have expired.
>
>How would I go about changing the account such that the password
>would never expire?
>The server has enhanced security.
>
>Thanks in advance for any advice.


The security manual has this to say on the subject.

7.5.4.1    Aging
If you do not want password aging on your system, in the default
database set u_exp and u_life to 0, and then (because of the way
the default methods of determining length restrictions on passwords
work based on the password lifetime) also set u_minlen and u_maxlen
to appropriate values for the site.

An example entry could be as follows:


 :u_exp#0:u_life#0:u_minlen#5:u_maxlen#32:\



Hope this helps
Adam Price

PS Cross posted to comp.unix.tru64
PPS This was taken from 4.0F Docs, but I don't think the information
has changed that much






