Moving to Tru64 from VMS(if you have to move from VMS) has several
advantages in that Compaq can offer many tools to ease the transition
and you may be able to keep some of the same hardware.
For scientific codes, if you can compile them yourself then DEC's
C and Fortran compilers are seen by many as excellent, and the alpha
is a very fast platform.
As for the 'standardness' of the unix implementation, Tru64 is pretty
much a bog standard 'BSD implementation, so most admins will have no
problems with it. It complies with most of the major unixy standards
like POSIX etc so the programmers shouldn't have any problem. If your
codes run on it then I would say go for it.

However since the requirement is to run a particular piece of commercial
scientific code I would suggest you talk to your code vendor and seek a
recommendation.

Hope this helps
Adam Price







