"Derek Bennetts" <user@nospam.co.uk> writes:


>    We have had this system running Tru64 4.0f for about a month now.
>Suddenly in the last week, I keep getting the message:-


>    chk_bf_quota: user quota underflow for user 224 on fileset /

>We do not have quotas turned on.

>Does anyone have any ideas on what is happening  ?

It's almost certainly a safe-to-ignore message, usually caused by
running ADVFS on the root filesystem with no quotas enabled. Typing
`user quota underflow' on the Tru64-Unix-Managers mailing list search
form (http://www-archive.ornl.gov:8000/) gives 106 hits, going back to
1996.

There are workarounds suggested on the mailing list, mostly revolving
around enabling quotas on / and running quotacheck; another workaround
is to ignore the messages (other than a reminder of how sloppy
DEC/Compaq can be), which is what we do.

