 >I have a Alpha Server 800 5/500 which boots to single-user mode every
>time.  I was told to hit Ctrl-D to get it to go on to multi-user mode.
>This works but I'd much rather not have to be there to do this if I need
>to reboot the machine while on the road or something.

From the console prompt (>>>), examine the current value of the console
enviroment variable "boot_osflags":

P00>>>show  boot_osflags
boot_osflags            a      

If the character "a" is not set, you will not boot multi-user.  To set
it:

P00>>>set boot_osflags a

and then boot.

Tony V.
Unix Base Kernel Group



