The COMPAQ people sell an Available Server Environment (ASE) as Part of the
TruCluster.

This uses shared disks via differential SCSI or a Shared
Dual ported HSZ such as ESA10000 or HSZ50 RAID
controller. It is not like a VMS Cluster as you cannot boot common system
disk.

You connect via SCSI bus and Ethernet/FDDI...

You should have multi-ethernets on each node. You can failover a cluster
member via the asemgr utility.

LSM is also supported in this package so you don't absolutely need Hardware
RAID.

I have setup a few VMS,DUNIX and NT clusters with and without RAID.

Steve


