this problem is in your makefile - search for CXX= it probably says CXX=c++,
Change it to CXX=cxx.  Suppose you should edit the configure script, but
I just wrote a quick sed script to change it in all the makefiles in all the
subdirs.  I assume you've installed the commercial C++ package.

Well, that seems to get around that problem, but then you'll get what I'm
currently getting:

syntax error on -W switch

I think I know what's going on with this, but haven't found the "right" place
to fix it yet.  The -W switch apparently is not acceptable with the Tru64 cc,
just gotta find the equivalent.  This appears to be -Wpassname,switch, but
well, I'm still digging :)

I'll email you if I get this working, just a little busy doing regular
sysadmin work right now, hehe.

