No, the reboot will not create new device files for you.  However, you will be
able to create the device files quite simply, even before the reboot:  CD to
/dev and issue the command

	./MAKEDEV rzN

where N = the SCSI ID of the disk you will install.  (It may work better if you
do it after the reboot, but it's not *necessary*.)

Have fun!

