Hi Stefan,

One problem you will have is finding a 1 inch 36GB disk that is
really shipping.  Be careful, because at least one company uses
LP to mean something other than Low Profile.  Also it is tough
to know what disk drive company will be around next year.  I
hear that Seagate is selling off their drives and have heard
rumors that with the right offer, Western Digital could be 
purchased.

I have ordered some 1 inch 36GB drives under the belief that 
they will work will 4.0f.  I have the SN-KZPCA-AA SCSI card
which supports the new faster lvd interface and ordered 68 pin
lvd type drives.  The lvd drives will also work with the old slower 
single ended scsi controllers.  (The SCSI people must have really
enjoyed naming lvd, low voltage differential, when it will not 
work with the older differential controllers, but will work with
the older single ended controllers!) By the way, the SN-KZPCA-AA
card has an external connector that can be used at the same time
that the internal connector is used.

Ray T.



